<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">July 12, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 135 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-07-12 07:00 UTC</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Early Knesset dissolution calendared July 17 (<span class="cite">F7</span>, <span class="cite">F8</span>) while the June 17 MOU framework (<span class="cite">F9</span>) confronts its sharpest military test since signing — Hormuz transits at 11/day after IRGC attacks, no confirmed ceasefire restoration, and the MOU's 60-day window expiring approximately August 17 (<span class="cite">F11</span>).
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active · last reasoned 2026-07-12 · Sunday cold-start audit run</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-Term (≤72h)</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Knesset pass the dissolution bill's final reading with a fixed election date earlier than 2026-10-27 before EOD 2026-07-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">5%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −40pp from 45% (2026-06-02)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Cold-start audit (Sunday): p_inherited=0.45, p_cold=0.05, gap=40pp — Judge selects cold-start p=0.05. Knesset legal adviser Sagit Afik formally recommended July 17 as dissolution date (2 days after the July 15 horizon) and October 27 as election date. Both resolution conditions fail simultaneously: (a) final reading scheduled July 17, not before July 15 EOD; (b) election date October 27 triggers ambiguity_rule "date on/after Oct 27 = NO."</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Knesset passes dissolution bill in final (third) reading AND specifies a fixed election date earlier than 2026-10-27, before EOD 2026-07-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Times of Israel/Reuters/AP/JPost) citing Knesset plenum vote record.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Preliminary/first/second readings without final passage = NO; passage with only a date band = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; date on/after Oct 27 = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Plenum third-reading dissolution vote with fixed date</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Haredi-coalition fixed September/Oct-20 date agreement</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Knesset formally dissolve (complete second and third readings of dissolution bill and issue dissolution proclamation) before EOD 2026-07-20?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">88%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ new</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-20</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Legal adviser Sagit Afik recommended July 17 dissolution date; first reading 106-0 with all coalition and opposition parties; scheduling confirmed by coalition chair. Risk scenarios for NO: Supreme Court injunction, haredi faction dispute over bill text, or procedural delay past July 20.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Knesset completes second and third readings of dissolution bill AND Speaker formally proclaims dissolution, confirmed by Knesset official record or government gazette, before EOD 2026-07-20.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Knesset official record (knesset.gov.il), Times of Israel, Jerusalem Post, Haaretz. Official proclamation or Speaker statement required.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Readings pass but proclamation issued after July 20 = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Bill passage without proclamation = NO. Court-ordered stay = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Knesset dissolution second and third readings</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Knesset legal adviser July 17 recommendation</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">First reading 106-0 unanimous vote (2026-06-02)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the June 17 US-Iran MOU framework remain formally in effect (not publicly suspended or terminated by either party) through EOD 2026-08-12?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">40%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ new</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-12</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. p=0.40 (reduced from initial 0.50 per DA partial-accept). IRGC maritime attacks July 6-7 triggered US retaliatory strikes; Hormuz transits fell to 11/day by July 10; Araghchi publicly stated US threats impede a final agreement. MOU faces severe stress but no formal government-level termination statement confirmed as of July 12. Counterweights: Doha back-channel active (Qatar, Pakistan), both parties' economic stakes, MOU's 60-day structured window expires ~August 17.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if neither US nor Iran has issued an official government statement formally suspending, abrogating, or declaring the June 17 MOU null and void by EOD 2026-08-12, AND at least one technical-level engagement under MOU framework confirmed by TIER1 during July 12–August 12.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1: Reuters, AP, CNN, Al Jazeera. Official US: White House or State Dept. Official Iran: IRNA or MFA. Both required for formal termination determination.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Conditional suspension (not formal termination) = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-YES. Both parties silent with no meetings AND no termination = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-YES. Unilateral IRGC action without government-level termination statement = does not alone trigger NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">IRGC maritime attacks July 6-7</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Araghchi "US threats" impediment statement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Qatar/Pakistan mediators active in Doha back-channel</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F12</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Gadi Eisenkot's Yashar party hold a seat projection equal to or greater than Likud's in the average of published Israeli election polls through EOD 2026-09-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">55%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ new</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Haaretz July 9: first poll where Eisenkot's Yashar (23 seats) exceeded Likud (20 seats) outright. Channel 12 July 7: both at 23. PM preference: Eisenkot 43% vs. Netanyahu 39% (Channel 13). Bennett Together at 15 seats. Opposition bloc projects 69 vs. coalition 51. Netanyahu exploring adding Smotrich to Likud reserved list amid fears Religious Zionist Party may fall below the 3.25% electoral threshold.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if simple average of three most recently published seat-projection polls (any TIER1 Israeli outlet) as of EOD 2026-09-01 shows Yashar ≥ Likud in projected seats. If fewer than three polls Aug 1–Sep 1, use all available.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1: Haaretz, Times of Israel, Jerusalem Post. Polling firms: Channel 12, Channel 13, Maariv, Panels Politics.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Yashar-Likud tie in average = YES. Eisenkot merges Yashar with another party = use combined projection. If Netanyahu removed and Likud rebrands/merges = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Fewer than two polls available = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">July 7-9 polls: Yashar 23 seats, Likud 20-23 seats</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Smotrich-Likud list merger talks active</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Bennett Together at 15 seats (centre-right fragmentation)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Strait of Hormuz 7-day average commercial transit count reach 40 or more vessels per day before EOD 2026-09-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">35%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ new</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Current transit level: 11/day as of July 10 (UANI; Bloomberg), down from 35 on July 7 following IRGC attacks on three commercial vessels and US retaliatory strikes. Pre-crisis baseline ~90/day. UK/France multinational MCM mission announced July 6, not yet commenced. Expert estimates: 40-50 days sustained MCM required before insurance companies restore coverage. Recovery to 40/day (44% of baseline) requires both sustained MCM and no further IRGC interdiction over 65 days.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if any TIER1 or named AIS source (IMF PortWatch, UANI, Windward AI, Lloyd's List) records a consecutive 7-day window averaging ≥40 commercial transits/day through Hormuz before EOD 2026-09-15. Naval vessels excluded.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1/OSINT: IMF PortWatch (portwatch.imf.org), UANI Iran Shipping Updates, Windward Daily Intelligence. At least one named outlet confirming 7-day average; single-day counts not sufficient.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>AIS-dark vessels excluded. Naval escorts count only if commercial vessels are confirmed transiting. If PortWatch unavailable, require two independent AIS sources. Single-day count of 40+ without confirmed 7-day average = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">UK/France multinational MCM mission commences</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Hormuz daily transit count 11/day (July 10)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC maritime attack recurrence</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F11</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US and Iran sign a comprehensive binding final agreement (substantively beyond the June 17 MOU, covering at minimum nuclear limits and sanctions) before EOD 2026-10-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">12%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ new</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Active obstacles: MOU's 60-day window expires approximately August 17; Hormuz transits near-standstill after July 6-7 attacks; Araghchi on record that US threats impede a final agreement; hardline Mojtaba Khamenei faction blocking Ghalibaf's diplomatic concessions; JCPOA formally terminated, UN sanctions reinstated; US demands on missiles and proxies not addressed in MOU. No principals-level meeting confirmed since July 1 Doha session.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if TIER1 confirms US and Iran formally signed a comprehensive bilateral agreement addressing at minimum: (a) specific uranium enrichment limits or dismantlement commitments AND (b) a defined sanctions relief architecture, publicly acknowledged by both governments.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1: Reuters, AP, BBC, CNN. Confirmed by both White House press office AND official Iranian government statement (IRNA or MFA) within same news cycle.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>MOU extension without comprehensive agreement = NO. Partial deal on one topic only = NO. Deal acknowledged by one party but not the other = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Framework setting future deadlines without binding commitments = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Araghchi "US threats" impediment statement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">MOU 60-day window expires approx. August 17</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Technical talks under MOU (last confirmed July 1 Doha)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 6-12 MONTHS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 Months</div>

